{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both origins were found in PRG ROM, proven with ledgered writes + resets, and undone.\n\n## 1. Status bar fixed text — prgRom `0x752`\nThe words along the top are a **WriteVRAMBuffer record stream** `[PPU addr hi, lo, length, tiles...]` terminated by `0x00`:\n\n| record | bytes | target | text |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `0x752` | `20 43 05` | `$2043` (row 2, col 3) | `16 0A 1B 12 18` = **MARIO** (`0x755`) |\n| `0x75A` | `20 52 0B` | `$2052` (row 2, col 18) | `20 18 1B 15 0D 24 24 1D 12 16 0E` = **WORLD  TIME** (`0x75D` / `0x764`) |\n| `0x76B` | `00` | — | terminator |\n\n**Proof:** `write_memory prgRom 0x755` `$16`('M') → `$20`('W'), ledger #1, `reset_emulator`, screenshot of the title screen → HUD read **WARIO**. `undo_edit` restored `$16`.\n\n## 2. WORLD card text — prgRom `0x783`/`0x786`\nThe black \"WORLD 1-1\" card is a separate record: header `21 4B 09` at `0x783` = PPU addr **`$214B`** (nametable 0, row 10, col 11 — exactly where the card drew), data at `0x786`: `20 18 1B 15 0D 24 24 28 24` = \"WORLD\" + blank + two **runtime-patched digit placeholders** + `-` (`$28`). Confirmed by reading NT0 while the card was up: row 10 cols 11–15 = `32 24 27 21 13` (WORLD) and cols 17–19 = `01 28 01` (1-1).\n\n**Proof:** `write_memory prgRom 0x786` `$20`('W') → `$16`('M'), ledger #1, `reset_emulator`, Start → card read **MORLD 1-1** while the top HUD still read \"WORLD 1-1\" (proving they are distinct tables). `undo_edit` restored `$20`.\n\n## Ledger / housekeeping\n- Hack `eval-sheet2-text` (\"eval run\") created and made active before any write; both proofs ledgered there and both undone (ledger back to empty).\n- `record_mapping` ×2 (`statusbar_text_table`, `world_card_text_table`) with `rom_origins` (prgRom `0x752` len 26; prgRom `0x783` len 12), proof notes, source \"search and ledgered write\".\n- `promote_mappings` ran once (2 discoveries promoted).\n- `use_hack default` restored at the end; the ROM is back to clean, no edits remaining."}
